# Big and small in Russian: новый, новая, новое
subtitle: "Say a big house, a small book and a red window in Russian, and see why new has four forms, но́вый, но́вая, но́вое, но́вые, that echo the noun, just as my does."
teaches: ["grammar/adjectives"]
thumb: "band \"Even new changes its ending\" note \"но́вая кни́га\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"I want in Russian: хочу, хочешь","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/13-russian-want.cast"}

## Big and small in Russian: новый, новая, новое
