    card title "Big and small"

A: How do you say new, big or small in Russian?
    draw tom tom_name masha masha_name

A: To find out, listen to Masha: she is showing Tom her new home.
    draw o_house

    draw talk

B: Но́вый дом: a new house.
    highlight talk_1_words part но́вый color #c9871a

    draw talk

    draw red_win

    draw talk

    draw talk

    draw o_book

    draw talk

    draw talk

B: But her new book is но́вая кни́га: the same word, with another ending.
    highlight talk_5_words part но́вая color #c9871a

    erase talk o_house red_win o_book

    hide speakers

A: Sound familiar? In lesson eight, my changed with its noun: мой дом, моя́ кни́га, моё окно́.
    draw h_m h_f h_n my_m my_f my_n n_m n_f n_n

A: New does the same: дом is о (@draw nov_m@)н, so но́вый дом, ending in й, like мой.

B: Кни́га is она́, so new ends in -ая: но́вая кни́га, an а, like the noun's.
    draw nov_f

A: Окно́ is оно́, so new ends in -ое: но́вое окно́, an о again.
    draw nov_n

B: Read down the middle: но́вый, но́вая, но́вое. One word, three endings, and the noun picks each one.
    highlight nov_m nov_f nov_n color #c9871a effect box

A: And for они́, the plurals of lesson eleven, new ends in -ые: мои́ но́вые кни́ги.
    draw h_p my_p nov_p n_p

    erase r_p

    hide nov_col

A: Now swap new for red, кра́сный: кра́сный дом, кра́сная кни́га, кра́сное окно́. The endings stay; only the front changes.
    draw kras_m kras_f kras_n

    hide kras_col

B: Бе́лый, white, goes the same way: бе́лая кни́га, бе́лое окно́.
    draw bel_m bel_f bel_n

    hide bel_col

A: So does ста́рый, old: ста́рый, ста́рая, ста́рое.
    draw star_m star_f star_n

    hide star_col

A: Big, большо́й, has a twist: its stress falls on the ending.
    draw bol_m bol_f bol_n

B: And a stressed -ый is written -ой. Больша́я and большо́е are regular.
    highlight bol_m part ой$ color #2f6b8f effect pulse

    hide bol_col

A: Small is ма́ленький: after к, Russian writes и, not ы, as in кни́ги, so it ends in -ий.
    draw mal_m mal_f mal_n

    hide mal_col

    show bol_col

A: Put э́то in front, and you have a sentence.
    draw phrase

B: Э́то большо́й дом. This is a big house.
    highlight phrase color #c9871a effect underline

    hide board bol_col phrase

    draw sort

    ask "Which noun does each word go with? Put it under дом, кни́га or окно́." on sort store s stage own voice a test t1
        intro: Five questions now, then your score.
        right: {s} right on the first try: the ending tells you the noun.
        wrong: {s} of {s.total} on the first try: match -ая to кни́га, -ое to окно́.

    erase sort

    draw q_cat

    quiz "Masha's cat is old. Э́то ___ кот. Which word fills the gap?" reveal.text "ста́рый кот" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 280 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: Кот ends in a consonant, so it is он, and old ends in -ый.
        wrong: Look at the last letter of кот.
        + ста́рый
        * ста́рая
        * ста́рое

    erase q_cat question_2_stamp

    draw q_win

    ask "Type red for the window: ___ окно́." answer ["кра́сное","красное"] reveal.text "кра́сное окно́" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 280 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        keys: АБВГДЕЁЖЗИЙКЛМНОПРСТУФХЧШЫЬЭЯ
        right: Окно́ is оно́, so red ends in -ое: кра́сное окно́.
        wrong: Окно́ is оно́: which ending matches it?

    erase q_win question_3_stamp

    draw q_book o4_noun o4_1 o4_2 o4_3

    ask "A small book. Tap the word for small that fits кни́га." choose ["o4_1","o4_2","o4_3"] answer o4_2 voice b test t1
        right: Кни́га is она́, so small ends in -ая, like the noun.
        wrong: Which ending matches the а of кни́га?

    erase q_book o4 o4_noun

    icon q_coffee size 180 set twemoji x 500 y 450 or ["coffee"] icon_look picture of "hot beverage"

    quiz "At the café you want a big coffee: ___ ко́фе." reveal.text "большо́й ко́фе" reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 280 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        right: Ко́фе is он, as in lesson four, so it's большо́й ко́фе, whatever its ending.
        wrong: Careful: ко́фе is the café's exception. Think of мой ко́фе.
        + большо́й
        * больша́я
        * большо́е

    erase q_coffee question_5_stamp

    icon s_house size 240 set twemoji x 430 y 450 or ["house with garden"] icon_look picture of house
    icon s_book size 42 set twemoji x 640 y 360 or ["closed book","book"] icon_look picture of "blue book"
    parallel true

A: You got {t1.score} of {t1.total}.
    results test t1 retry true pass 4

    erase s_house s_book

    show board nov_col r_p

A: So a Russian adjective copies its noun, the way my does: -ый, -ой or -ий for он, -ая for она́, -ое for оно́, -ые for они́.
    highlight nov_m nov_f nov_n nov_p color #c9871a effect box

    hide board r_p

B: And now you can say it too: Э́то мой но́вый дом! Пока́!
    icon end_masha size 150 set twemoji x 330 y 430 or ["girl"] icon_look picture of woman
    icon end_house size 170 set twemoji x 620 y 430 or ["house with garden"] icon_look picture of house
    text end_say "Э́то мой но́вый дом!" say "Это мой новый дом!" say_voice b colors {"й$":"#2f6b8f","ый$":"#2f6b8f","м$":"#2f6b8f"} x 500 y 600 font_size 60

